  {
   "id": "sec2-16",
   "section": "Case history",
   "text": "On October 17, 2024, the court \"stated that the ban’s exceptions are vague and confusing; outlined specific conditions under which abortion care is permitted under the state’s ban; and held that the Center would likely succeed on its constitutional claims, which include that the ban violates pregnant patients’ right to life and equal protection under the law and is unconstitutionally vague\".",
   "words": 63,
   "authors": [
